---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MathCard from '../components/MathCard.astro';
import Marquee from '../components/Marquee.astro';

const plan = [
	'Measure the extractable value in a trade, on-chain, before it settles.',
	'Auction it at second price, so bidding an honest belief is what wins.',
	'Return the proceeds to the swapper and the liquidity providers.',
];

const parameters = [
	['MIN_STAKE', '0.1 ETH', 'Bond an arbitrageur posts before any quote of theirs counts as live.'],
	['MAX_ACTIVE_QUOTERS', '32', 'Per pool. Caps the loop the hook walks inside beforeSwap.'],
	['MAX_QUOTE_DURATION', '5 minutes', 'Longest a belief stays valid. Stale prices expire themselves.'],
	['Hook permissions', 'beforeSwap · afterSwap · afterSwapReturnDelta', 'The three flags mined into the hook address.'],
];

const without = [
	'A searcher sees your swap coming and moves ahead of it.',
	'They decide on their own what the position in front of you is worth.',
	'Whatever they take out, they keep.',
	'You find out what it cost you by reading your own fill.',
];

const with_ = [
	'A searcher still moves ahead of it. That part does not change.',
	'The pool makes them outbid everyone else who wanted the same spot.',
	'They hand over what the next bidder would have paid.',
	'That payment lands back in your trade before it settles.',
];

const cards = [
	{
		title: 'We stopped trying to hide',
		body: 'Most answers to this ask you to trust something new — a private relay, an encrypted mempool, someone’s reputation. We took the opposite bet and assumed your trade is visible to everyone, because it usually is.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We turned a toll into a market',
		body: 'One searcher standing in front of your trade is a tax with no ceiling. A dozen of them competing for that spot is an auction, and auctions have a clearing price you can actually reason about.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We made honesty the winning move',
		body: 'Whoever wins pays what the runner-up offered, never their own number. Quote below what you think it is worth and you gain nothing — you just lose the trades you wanted.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We sent the money home',
		body: 'Nothing leaves through a side door. What gets paid goes back into the pool it came from: to the person who made the trade, or to the people whose liquidity absorbed it.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Hyberbola"
	description="A Uniswap v4 hook that auctions the MEV in every trade and returns it to swappers and LPs."
>
	<MathCard />

	<main>
		<header class="bar">
			<span class="mark">Hyberbola</span>
		</header>

		<section class="hero">
			<div class="headline-wrap">
				<Marquee />
				<h1>We are building the hook that gives <em>the sandwich back.</em></h1>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="prose">
			<p>
				Every trade that moves a constant-product pool carries extractable value, and today it
				goes to whoever is fastest. Blocking that has been tried from every direction — private
				relays, encrypted mempools, fee surcharges — and each one asks you to trust something
				new. None of them change the fact that the value exists.
			</p>
			<p>
				So do not fight it. Price it. The card on the right measures exactly how much value a
				trade holds, then hands it to whoever will pay the most for it — and routes that payment
				straight back into the pool it came from.
			</p>
			<p>
				The value is not an estimate. It falls out of the pool's own invariant, it is computed
				on-chain before the swap settles, and it is bounded above by a quantity anyone can check.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="plan">
			<ol>
				{
					plan.map((item, i) => (
						<li>
							<span class="num">{i + 1}</span>
							<span>{item}</span>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="prose">
			<p>
				Hyberbola is a Uniswap v4 hook. Arbitrageurs stake, then post the price they actually
				believe a pair is worth. When a swap arrives, the hook scores every live belief against
				that specific trade, and the highest bidder wins the right to run the bundle — the
				front-run, the user's swap, and the unwind, all inside one atomic callback.
			</p>
			<p>
				The winner pays the runner-up's valuation rather than their own, so there is nothing to
				gain from shading a bid. What they pay does not leave the pool: on the trade path it
				settles back to the swapper as a refund, and on the rebalancing path it is donated
				directly to liquidity providers.
			</p>
			<p>
				What the winner keeps is only the distance between the best belief and the second-best.
				Add arbitrageurs and that margin compresses. The extraction never stops — it just stops
				being a transfer away from the people who created the trade.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="params">
			<h2>Parameters, as deployed</h2>
			<dl>
				{
					parameters.map(([name, value, note]) => (
						<div class="param">
							<dt>{name}</dt>
							<dd class="param-value">{value}</dd>
							<dd class="param-note">{note}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section class="quote">
			<blockquote>The MEV was never the problem. Who kept it was.</blockquote>
		</section>

		<section class="versus">
			<h2>Same trade, two worlds</h2>
			<div class="versus-grid">
				<div class="versus-col">
					<span class="versus-label">On an ordinary pool</span>
					<ol>
						{without.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
					</ol>
				</div>
				<div class="versus-col versus-col-lit">
					<span class="versus-label">On this one</span>
					<ol>
						{with_.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
					</ol>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="cards">
			<h2>What we did</h2>
			<div class="card-grid">
				{
					cards.map((card) => (
						<article class="ecard">
							<h3>{card.title}</h3>
							<p>{card.body}</p>
						</article>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="status">
			<h2>Status</h2>
			<p>
				The contracts are written and tested. Nothing is deployed to a public network yet, so
				there is no address to give you and no audit to point at. The hook console reads whatever
				deployment you point it at, including a local anvil node.
			</p>
			<p>
				One known issue: with zero active liquidity the limit-state calculation divides by the raw
				liquidity value, which reverts the swap. It is reachable whenever every position sits
				outside the current tick.
			</p>
			<a class="cta" href="/dashboard">Open the hook console →</a>
		</section>

		<footer>
			<span class="dim">Uniswap v4 hook · MIT</span>
			<a href="/dashboard">Hook console</a>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		width: var(--col-left);
		padding: 0 var(--step-6) 0 var(--step-5);
	}

	section {
		padding-bottom: var(--step-7);
	}

	.bar {
		padding: var(--step-4) 0 0;
	}

	.mark {
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: 20px;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.hero {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: calc(100vh - var(--step-6));
		padding-bottom: var(--step-6);
	}

	.headline-wrap {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
	}

	h1 {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		max-width: 22ch;
		font-size: var(--hl-size);
		line-height: var(--hl-lead);
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}

	h1 em {
		font-style: normal;
		color: #d9a066;
	}

	.prose p + p {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
	}

	.prose p {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.plan ol li {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 62ch;
		padding: var(--step-2) 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.plan ol li:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.num {
		flex: none;
		width: 1.5rem;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	h2 {
		margin-bottom: var(--step-4);
		font-size: var(--type-body);
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	dl {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.param {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 15rem 1fr;
		gap: 2px var(--step-3);
		padding: var(--step-2) 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.param:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	dt {
		grid-row: span 2;
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: 13px;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	dd {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.param-note {
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.quote blockquote {
		max-width: 20ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 36px);
		line-height: 1.2;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.versus-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.versus-col {
		padding: var(--step-3);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	.versus-col-lit {
		border-color: rgba(217, 160, 102, 0.35);
		background: rgba(217, 160, 102, 0.045);
	}

	.versus-label {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: var(--step-3);
		font-size: 12px;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.versus-col-lit .versus-label {
		color: #d9a066;
	}

	.versus-col ol {
		counter-reset: step;
	}

	.versus-col li {
		position: relative;
		padding: 0 0 var(--step-3) var(--step-4);
		counter-increment: step;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.versus-col li:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
	}

	.versus-col li::before {
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		content: counter(step);
		color: var(--ink-faint);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.versus-col-lit li {
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.card-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.ecard {
		padding: var(--step-3);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 12px;
		transition: border-color 200ms ease;
	}

	.ecard:hover {
		border-color: #3d3d3d;
	}

	.ecard h3 {
		margin-bottom: var(--step-2);
		font-size: 17px;
		font-weight: 300;
		letter-spacing: -0.015em;
	}

	.ecard p {
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.dim {
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.status p {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.status p + p {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
	}

	.cta {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: var(--step-4);
		padding-bottom: 3px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.cta:hover {
		border-color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.fine {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 46ch;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	footer {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--step-5);
		padding: var(--step-4) 0 var(--step-5);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	footer a:last-child {
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		main {
			width: auto;
			padding: 0 var(--gap) calc(var(--card-h) + var(--step-4));
		}

		.hero {
			min-height: calc(100vh - var(--card-h) - var(--step-5));
		}

		section {
			padding-bottom: var(--step-6);
		}

		.param {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}

		dt {
			grid-row: auto;
		}

		.versus-grid,
		.card-grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
